{
  "_note": [
    "The one language table. public/js/languages.mjs, server/languages.mjs,",
    "server/languages.py, server/translate.py and server/llmTranslate.mjs all",
    "read this file, so there is nothing to keep in sync by hand (#32). It lives",
    "under public/ because the browser fetches it as a JSON module; the servers",
    "read it off disk.",
    "",
    "One row per language, one line per row, so adding a language touches only",
    "its own line (docs/adding-a-language.md). Fields:",
    "",
    "code     — the app's code for it (ISO 639-1).",
    "name     — shown in the translate bar and given to the chat model in prompts.",
    "nllb     — the Flores-200 code NLLB expects. Its suffix (_Latn, _Cyrl, …) is",
    "           the script, which picks the OCR model (server/languages.py).",
    "offered  — true once all three gates (translation, transcription, OCR) have",
    "           been checked. Offered languages are what can be studied — an",
    "           import in any other language is refused with a clear message —",
    "           and what the translate bar lists. With no row offered, every",
    "           language is.",
    "whisper  — Whisper's code when it differs from `code` (Norwegian is `no`",
    "           there); null when Whisper can't transcribe it at all.",
    "ocr      — overrides the script's OCR recognition model (a RapidOCR",
    "           lang_type); null when no model reads it, so caption OCR is",
    "           skipped instead of returning look-alike garbage.",
    "inaudible — the placeholder shown over speech Whisper couldn't make out,",
    "           in the language itself; \"(…)\" when absent."
  ],
